    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0159" n="141" xml:id="pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/2–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-11T19:00:00-05:00">February 11,
                            1947—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>698. We have been following with concern recent developments in India<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d88-f1"/> and would appreciate info re Brit thinking as to
                    next steps. If you have opportunity we hope you will endeavor to ascertain
                    whether or not Brit are disposed to instruct Viceroy dismiss Muslim League
                    members from Council, whether they are planning to bring pressure on Princes to
                    reach definitive agreement with Congress and whether they have been giving
                    consideration to possibility of meeting problem Muslim League absence from
                    Constituent Assembly by modifying Cabinet Mission plan to include provision for
                    provincial ratification (either by popular plebiscite or legislative action) of
                    constitutions drafted by Assembly.</p>
                <p>Sent London 698 rptd New Delhi 77.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d88-f1" n="1" xml:id="d88-f1-content">
                <p>On, February 5, the Congress and minority members of the Interim Government,
                    reacting to the League’s resolution of January 31 (see telegram 5, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>), had presented the Viceroy with a demand for
                    the resignation of the Muslim League representatives.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
